# Line-ending policy.
#
# statusgen reads the board's inputs — STATUS.md, CLAUDE.md, and everything under
# docs/streams/** — and `statusgen --lint` compares them byte-for-byte against a fresh
# regeneration. A default Windows checkout (git autocrlf) rewrites those files with CRLF
# on checkout, so the windows-latest CI leg (windows-port/04) reddened `statusgen --lint`
# while Linux passed on the identical tree. Pinning the board's inputs to LF on checkout
# keeps a Windows working tree byte-identical to Linux. (#584)
*.md            text eol=lf
docs/streams/** text eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts keep their CRLF endings.
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
*.psm1 text eol=crlf
